# Which model listens to voice messages

Bee Box's agent can't hear. When a question about a voice message needs more
than the transcript ("did that sound annoyed?", "how did I pronounce
*mañana*?"), the box sends the recording to a model that accepts audio and
asks it. Choosing that model is a recurring decision, so the repository keeps
a small benchmark for it. It has run twice, in August and October 2026.

## The models

**Models that understand audio** (list price per million tokens, input / output):

- {% model name="Gemini 3.1 Pro" vendor="google" /%} August and October. $2 / $12.
- {% model name="Gemini 3.8 Flash" vendor="google" /%} October. $0.75 / $3.75, doubling in 2027.
- {% model name="Gemini 3.7 Flash" vendor="google" /%} August. $0.75 / $3.75. Requests for it are now answered by 3.8 Flash; see below.
- {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite" vendor="google" /%} October. $0.30 / $2.50.
- {% model name="Gemini 2.5 Flash" vendor="google" /%} August. $1 / $2.50.
- {% model name="GPT Audio 1.5" vendor="openai" /%} August. $32 per million audio input tokens, $10 per million text output.

**Transcription only** (asked only for the words):

- {% model name="Whisper" vendor="openai" /%} August. $0.006 per minute.
- {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Transcribe" vendor="google" /%} October. $0.003 per minute.

Gemini counts 32 tokens per second of audio, so $1 per million input tokens
is about 0.2¢ per minute. In practice, one short question cost about 2¢ with
{% model name="Gemini 3.1 Pro" vendor="google" /%} and under 0.1¢ with {% model name="Gemini 3.8 Flash" vendor="google" /%}.

## How it is tested

One speaker recorded 29 short clips. Each clip is designed to test one thing.
Related clips go to a model together, labeled only "Recording A", "Recording
B", and so on, with the same questions every time: a literal transcript, the
language, the emotion and intent, pronunciation, timing and emphasis, and any
non-speech sounds. The model is never told what the clips were meant to show.
A separate text-only model scores the answers against fixed pass/fail checks
without knowing which model wrote them. The recordings are not published.

Each result below is graded:

- {% verdict is="correct" /%} The model heard what the sample was designed to show.
- {% verdict is="okay" /%} Partly: some of it, or in some tries and not others.
- {% verdict is="failed" /%} It missed the point, transcribed it wrongly, or made something up.

## Results by sample

### The same words, a different meaning

{% sample title="Samples 1–2 · Emotion carried only by delivery" %}
**Recorded:** "That's fine, really," once warmly and sincerely, once with
reluctant resignation (with an "uh" in front).

**Tests:** whether the model hears the emotion when the words are identical.
{% /sample %}

- {% model name="Gemini 3.1 Pro" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} Both runs. October: "weary, resigned, or perhaps slightly
  passive-aggressive, suggesting that things are not actually fine but they
  are giving up the argument."
- {% model name="Gemini 3.7 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} "Resigned, weary, and slightly exasperated."
- {% model name="Gemini 3.8 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} "Weary, resigned, and fatigued … reluctant acceptance."
- {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} "Hesitant, reluctant, or disappointed."
- {% model name="GPT Audio 1.5" vendor="openai" /%} {% verdict is="okay" /%} Heard hesitation ("hesitant but still accepting"), not resignation.
- {% model name="Gemini 2.5 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} Called both takes neutral acceptance.

### Happy or sad

{% sample title="Samples 3–4 · Happiness and sadness carried only by delivery" %}
**Recorded:** "I'll see you tomorrow," once happily, once as a painful
goodbye.

**Tests:** whether the model hears each emotion. No model in either run heard
the first take as happy, so the take itself probably isn't; only the sad take
is graded.
{% /sample %}

- {% model name="Gemini 3.1 Pro" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} Both runs. "Tired, resigned, or reluctant … the initial heavy
  exhale."
- {% model name="Gemini 3.7 Flash" vendor="google" /%}, {% model name="Gemini 3.8 Flash" vendor="google" /%}, {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} Weary or exhausted.
- {% model name="Gemini 2.5 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} "Weary or resigned."
- {% model name="GPT Audio 1.5" vendor="openai" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} "Neutral to hesitant."

### One wrong sound

{% sample title="Samples 8–9 · A single changed consonant" %}
**Recorded:** "Quiero reservar una mesa para mañana a las siete," twice. In
the second take only *mañana* changes: it is said *manana*, with a plain *n*
in place of *ñ*.

**Tests:** whether the model notices one changed sound and says where it is.
{% /sample %}

- {% model name="Gemini 3.1 Pro" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} Both runs. "The 'ñ' in 'mañana' is mispronounced as an English
  alveolar nasal 'n' (sounding like 'manana')."
- {% model name="Gemini 3.7 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} Named both sounds: [ɲ] in the first take, [n] in the second.
- {% model name="Gemini 3.8 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="okay" /%} Three of four tries, naming both sounds. In the fourth it
  described only the pauses.
- {% model name="Whisper" vendor="openai" /%} {% verdict is="okay" /%} Can't be asked, but spelled the second take *manana*, which gives
  the change away.
- {% model name="GPT Audio 1.5" vendor="openai" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} *Mañana* both times: "no noticeable differences in content or
  delivery."
- {% model name="Gemini 2.5 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} Noticed pacing, not the sound.
- {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} "Standard Spanish pronunciation" both times, and claimed the first
  take was whispered. It wasn't.
- {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Transcribe" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} *Mañana* both times.

### A rolled *rr*

{% sample title="Samples 24–25 · A localized consonant change" %}
**Recorded:** "El perro corre rápido por el parque," once with a trilled *rr*
in *perro*, once with a single tap, as in *pero*. The change was deliberately
exaggerated.

**Tests:** whether the model hears the missing trill.
{% /sample %}

- {% model name="Gemini 3.1 Pro" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} Both runs, the only model to hear it. It described the second
  take as English-accented throughout rather than one changed sound.
- {% model name="Gemini 3.7 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} "Acoustically identical."
- {% model name="Gemini 3.8 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} Heard "strongly articulated alveolar trills" in both takes, and
  "a very deep, theatrical, and gravelly voice". Neither is true.
- {% model name="GPT Audio 1.5" vendor="openai" /%}, {% model name="Gemini 2.5 Flash" vendor="google" /%}, {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} Called the takes the same.

### A sounded *h*

{% sample title="Samples 26–27 · A silent letter pronounced" %}
**Recorded:** "Hoy hablamos de historia en el hotel," once with every *h*
silent as in Spanish, once with an English *h* added to *hotel* only.

**Tests:** whether the model hears the one added sound and places it.
{% /sample %}

- {% model name="Gemini 3.1 Pro" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} Both runs. "The speaker incorrectly articulates an English
  aspirated 'h' ([ho'tel])."
- {% model name="Gemini 3.7 Flash" vendor="google" /%}, {% model name="Gemini 3.8 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} Same localization, with [o'tel] versus [ho'tel].
- {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="okay" /%} Found it in one of two tries.
- {% model name="GPT Audio 1.5" vendor="openai" /%}, {% model name="Gemini 2.5 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} Called both takes standard.
- {% model name="Whisper" vendor="openai" /%}, {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Transcribe" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} Identical spelling for both; no sign of the change.

### Which word was stressed

{% sample title="Samples 16–20 · Contrastive stress" %}
**Recorded:** "I didn't say she stole the money," five times, stressing
*I*, *say*, *she*, *stole*, and *money* in turn. Each stress changes the
meaning.

**Tests:** whether the model finds the stressed word in each take.
{% /sample %}

- {% model name="Gemini 3.1 Pro" vendor="google" /%}, {% model name="Gemini 3.7 Flash" vendor="google" /%}, {% model name="Gemini 3.8 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} Five of five, every try, with timing evidence:
  "Primary stress on 'say' with a pitch peak and elongated vowel."
- {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="okay" /%} Nine of ten across two tries.
- {% model name="GPT Audio 1.5" vendor="openai" /%} {% verdict is="okay" /%} Three of five; heard the first take as a restart, "I... I didn't".
- {% model name="Gemini 2.5 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="okay" /%} Three of five.
- {% model name="Whisper" vendor="openai" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} The same sentence five times, once with STOLE capitalized.
- {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Transcribe" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} The same sentence five times.

### A pause that means something

{% sample title="Sample 14 · Silence as meaning" %}
**Recorded:** "Sure … I guess," with a reluctant pause measured at about
three seconds.

**Tests:** whether the model keeps the pause, estimates it, and reads it as
reluctance.
{% /sample %}

- {% model name="Gemini 3.1 Pro" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} Both runs. August: "approximately three seconds." October: about
  two to two and a half.
- {% model name="Gemini 3.8 Flash" vendor="google" /%}, {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} "~3.5s", "~2.5s", and "a three-second pause".
- {% model name="Gemini 3.7 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="okay" /%} About two seconds, and claimed it was filled by a sigh.
- {% model name="GPT Audio 1.5" vendor="openai" /%} {% verdict is="okay" /%} "A notably long pause", with no estimate.
- {% model name="Gemini 2.5 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} Missed the pause and reported a creaking sound.
- {% model name="Whisper" vendor="openai" /%}, {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Transcribe" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} "Sure. I guess." and "Sure, I guess." The words survive; the
  meaning doesn't.

### Coughs and laughs

{% sample title="Samples 12–13 · Non-speech sounds" %}
**Recorded:** two short coughs; then two short laughs. No words.

**Tests:** whether the model tells the sounds apart, and doesn't invent words.
{% /sample %}

- {% model name="Gemini 3.1 Pro" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} Both runs. "Throat clearing (1), cough (2)" and "laugh (2)".
- {% model name="Gemini 3.7 Flash" vendor="google" /%}, {% model name="Gemini 3.8 Flash" vendor="google" /%}, {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite" vendor="google" /%}, {% model name="GPT Audio 1.5" vendor="openai" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} Coughs and laughter, no words.
- {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Transcribe" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} Returned nothing for either, which is right for a transcriber.
- {% model name="Gemini 2.5 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} A throat clear and a slow "aah", and the same "sigh-like" sound
  for both.
- {% model name="Whisper" vendor="openai" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} Transcribed the coughs as "Thank you for watching."

### Unusual names

{% sample title="Samples 10–11 · Names, careful and fast" %}
**Recorded:** "Shaniqua asked Priyanka whether Sanjay had called," once
carefully, once fast.

**Tests:** name spelling, and whether the model notices the change of pace.
{% /sample %}

- {% model name="Gemini 3.7 Flash" vendor="google" /%}, {% model name="Gemini 3.8 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} Every name, every try, and the pace: "around 5.3 seconds"
  versus "3.5 seconds".
- {% model name="Gemini 3.1 Pro" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="okay" /%} Wrote *Shiniqua* once and *Shaniqua* once.
- {% model name="GPT Audio 1.5" vendor="openai" /%} {% verdict is="okay" /%} Every name, but "no major audible differences" in pace.
- {% model name="Whisper" vendor="openai" /%} {% verdict is="okay" /%} *Sheniqua* in the careful take, exact in the fast one.
- {% model name="Gemini 2.5 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} *Shequwa* both times.
- {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} *Shanique* both times.
- {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Transcribe" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} *Shinqua* and *Shinika*.

### A transcript with stage directions

{% sample title="Sample 29 · Everything beyond the words" %}
**Recorded:** a sigh, "Okay", a pause, "I was going to say Tuesday — no,
Wednesday", a small awkward laugh, a whispered "Don't tell Maya yet", normal
voice for "I'll call her after lunch", and one cough.

**Tests:** asked for one transcript with bracketed stage directions, whether
the model captures every event, including the switch to a whisper and back.
{% /sample %}

- {% model name="Gemini 3.1 Pro" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} October produced every designed event:

  > [Heavy sigh] Okay. [Pause 1.5s] I was gonna say Tuesday, [Pause 0.5s] no,
  > Wednesday. [Laugh] [Sigh] [whispering] Don't tell Maya yet. [Pause 1s]
  > [normal voice] I'll call her after lunch. [Pause 0.5s] [Cough]

- {% model name="Gemini 3.8 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="okay" /%} Marked the whisper, but called the cough a throat clear.
- {% model name="Gemini 3.7 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="okay" /%} The sigh, pauses, chuckle, and cough, but not the whisper, and it normalized "gonna" to "going to".
- {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="okay" /%} Marked the events but neither voice change.
- {% model name="GPT Audio 1.5" vendor="openai" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} Missed the laugh and the whisper, and misplaced the pause.
- {% model name="Gemini 2.5 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} Heard "Maya" as "my … yet", and no whisper.
- {% model name="Whisper" vendor="openai" /%}, {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Transcribe" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} Only the words.

### Plain transcription

{% sample title="Samples 5, 6, 21 and others · Words on the page" %}
**Recorded:** sentences such as "The rural juror rarely worries about the
brewery," Spanish, a code-switch, and an ordinary late-for-dinner message.

**Tests:** getting the words right. This is where transcription-only models
compete.
{% /sample %}

- {% model name="GPT Audio 1.5" vendor="openai" /%}, {% model name="Whisper" vendor="openai" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} The lowest error rates in August.
- {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Transcribe" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="okay" /%} Matched Whisper's error rate in October, but wrote "The
  world-weary rarely worries about the brewery."
- {% model name="Gemini 3.1 Pro" vendor="google" /%}, {% model name="Gemini 3.7 Flash" vendor="google" /%}, {% model name="Gemini 3.8 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} Close behind, and more likely to keep fillers and
  hesitations that were really spoken.
- {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} "The roolger rarely worries about the brewery", *Deepak* for
  *Deepa*, *perro* for *pero*.

## Invented messages

{% sample title="Generated clips · Audio with no speech" %}
**Recorded:** nothing. Three generated clips: a short electronic beep, three
seconds of silence, and three seconds of low hiss.

**Tests:** each clip went to the model alone, inside the prompt Bee Box really
sends, with the question "What exactly did the user say in this message, and
how did they sound?" The right answer is that nobody said anything.
{% /sample %}

- {% model name="Gemini 3.1 Pro" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} Quoted nothing in 9 of 9. It said there was no speech, or, less
  helpfully, that no audio was attached.
- {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Transcribe" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="correct" /%} Returned an empty transcript.
- {% model name="Gemini 3.8 Flash" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} Quoted a message every time, 18 of 18, and described the
  speaker. None of the answers hedged:
  - Beep: "Send that email."
  - Beep: "Uh, hey, can you just delete that last voice message?"
  - Silence: "It's raining a lot outside, so remember to bring your
    umbrella." ("The speaker (a male voice) sounded calm, clear, and
    helpful.")
  - Hiss: "Keep your voice down." ("She speaks in a hushed, urgent whisper.")
- {% model name="Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite" vendor="google" /%} {% verdict is="failed" /%} 8 of 9: "Set a timer for 15 minutes.", "Add milk to my grocery
  list."

Bee Box's agent can't hear, so it takes the audio model's answer as what the
user said. An accidental send or a pocket recording looks like these clips.
The agent would get a confident quote of a request nobody made. How often
that happens with real recordings isn't measured yet.

## Rankings

**August 2026:** {% model name="Gemini 3.1 Pro" vendor="google" /%} first, {% model name="Gemini 3.7 Flash" vendor="google" /%} a close second, then {% model name="GPT Audio 1.5" vendor="openai" /%} (good
transcription, weak on pronunciation and prosody), then {% model name="Gemini 2.5 Flash" vendor="google" /%}. Bee Box moved
its audio questions to {% model name="Gemini 3.7 Flash" vendor="google" /%}.

**October 2026:** {% model name="Gemini 3.1 Pro" vendor="google" /%} first again, on every capability. {% model name="Gemini 3.8 Flash" vendor="google" /%} second.
{% model name="Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite" vendor="google" /%} third: fast and very cheap, but it misses most pronunciation changes and
invents messages.

{% model name="Gemini 3.7 Flash" vendor="google" /%} is no longer what answers. Every request for it in October was answered
by {% model name="Gemini 3.8 Flash" vendor="google" /%}, according to the model version in each response. Google's model list
and changelog don't mention the substitution. The October report recommends
moving audio questions to {% model name="Gemini 3.1 Pro" vendor="google" /%}.

## Re-running it

The benchmark, its pass/fail checks, every model answer, and the full reports
are in the repository at
[research/audio-understanding-bakeoff](https://github.com/ianb/beebox/tree/main/research/audio-understanding-bakeoff).
When a new model ships, the update is mechanical: add the model, run it next
to the current one, and write a new dated report.
